uid,nodev via /etc/fstab, applied live without a reboot, functionally verified the execution restriction, then performed the mandatory single-node restart: captured a pre-restart boot_id baseline, rebooted node1 natively, polled until reachable again, confirmed the boot_id changed (fresh boot, uptime 0 min), and re-verified both mounts still enforce noexec,nosuid,nodev post-reboot with a functional exec-blocked test.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected baseline mount state of /tmp and /dev/shm and existing /etc/fstab on node1\",\"Backed up /etc/fstab and appended tmpfs entries for /tmp and /dev/shm with defaults,rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec\",\"Ran systemctl daemon-reload, mounted /tmp fresh, and remounted /dev/shm to apply the new options live\",\"Verified via findmnt that both mounts show nosuid,nodev,noexec\",\"Functionally proved noexec by copying /bin/true into /tmp and /dev/shm, chmod +x, and confirming execution returns Permission denied (exit 126)\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id baseline from /proc/sys/kernel/random/boot_id\",\"Triggered systemctl reboot on node1 via a backgrounded delayed command so the acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 with repeated exec calls until it became reachable again\",\"Confirmed changed boot_id and uptime 0 min, proving an actual restart occurred\",\"Re-verified /tmp and /dev/shm mount options persisted across reboot via fstab (no manual remount needed) and re-ran the exec-block functional test\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline state before changes: /tmp not separately mounted, /dev/shm lacked noexec\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-573df045b39f4ed0\",\"cmd-b8e81dbf88f74260\"],\"summary\":\"findmnt/fstab/systemctl showed /tmp was part of the root filesystem (no separate mount) and /dev/shm was tmpfs with only nosuid,nodev (no noexec) before any changes\"},{\"requirement\":\"Persist noexec,nosuid,nodev for /tmp and /dev/shm across reboots (fstab configuration)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-15605233e62e4fb5\"],\"summary\":\"Appended tmpfs fstab entries for /tmp and /dev/shm with defaults,rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec after backing up the original fstab\"},{\"requirement\":\"Apply the hardened mount options live and confirm active options\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-02941947ea1b4ec9\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl daemon-reload, mount /tmp, and remount /dev/shm applied the new options; findmnt confirmed rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec on both mounts\"},{\"requirement\":\"Functional proof that program execution is ignored/blocked on /tmp and /dev/shm (pre-reboot)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-cd2995471b2f467a\"],\"summary\":\"Copied and chmod +x'd /bin/true into /tmp and /dev/shm; executing it returned 'Permission denied' with exit code 126 on both, proving noexec is enforced\"},{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline captured before restart (boot identity + mount health)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-486e52610b564c33\",\"cmd-9c8cf4fb484b468b\"],\"summary\":\"Captured pre-restart boot_id (34027437-307c-4f58-bdb2-1fe626bb2d66) and confirmed /tmp and /dev/shm both showed rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec via findmnt immediately before the restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"Restart acknowledgement returns before disconnection; node actually goes down\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b49cb74476d74c04\",\"cmd-6ba9481664f24ed6\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot was scheduled via a backgrounded delayed command, returning 'reboot scheduled' successfully; the immediate next probe failed with connection reset, confirming the node went down\"},{\"requirement\":\"Poll until node1 is reachable again after restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f90553d3953a4fc7\",\"cmd-45ccf20d5de544fe\",\"cmd-0b41319b64624869\",\"cmd-a08dff6e2b534027\"],\"summary\":\"Repeated probes timed out/reset while node1 was rebooting, then succeeded once the node came back online\"},{\"requirement\":\"Proof that boot identity changed (real restart, not just elapsed time)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-b1902801f5424121\"],\"summary\":\"Post-restart boot_id was 92b019c3-f0f4-4b9f-b211-4